## 3. Global Confusion Matrix & Core Metrics

### 3.1 Global 2x2 Matrix

```
                        Actual Class (Ground Truth)
                       ┌─────────────────┬─────────────────┐
                       │  High-Rate (P)  │   Normal (N)    │
     ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┼─────────────────┤
     │ Predicted       │  True Positive  │ False Positive  │
     │ Anomaly (Pos)   │     (TP): [ ]   │     (FP): [ ]   │
Pred ├─────────────────┼─────────────────┼─────────────────┤
     │ Predicted       │ False Negative  │  True Negative  │
     │ Normal (Neg)    │     (FN): [ ]   │     (TN): [ ]   │
     └─────────────────┴─────────────────┴─────────────────┘
```

### 3.2 Metric Definitions & Calculations

| Metric | Formula | Value | Notes / Implications |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **True Positive Rate (TPR / Recall)** | $\frac{\text{TP}}{\text{TP} + \text{FN}}$ | `[0.00%]` | Percentage of malicious/high-rate windows successfully caught. |
| **False Positive Rate (FPR)** | $\frac{\text{FP}}{\text{FP} + \text{TN}}$ | `[0.00%]` | Percentage of legitimate normal windows incorrectly flagged. |
| **Specificity (True Negative Rate)** | $\frac{\text{TN}}{\text{TN} + \text{FP}}$ | `[0.00%]` | Ability to reject legitimate vehicle communication without alarm. |
| **Precision (Positive Predictive Value)**| $\frac{\text{TP}}{\text{TP} + \text{FP}}$ | `[0.00%]` | Reliability of an anomaly alert when triggered. |
| **F1-Score** | $2 \times \frac{\text{Precision} \times \text{Recall}}{\text{Precision} + \text{Recall}}$ | `[0.0000]` | Harmonic mean of precision and detection sensitivity. |
| **Balanced Accuracy** | $\frac{\text{TPR} + \text{TNR}}{2}$ | `[0.00%]` | Unbiased accuracy across balanced/imbalanced traffic streams. |

