$$\Delta_s = \min(s_{\text{normal}}) - \max(s_{\text{attack}})$$

* **Observed Separation Margin ($\Delta_s$):** `[0.0000]`
* **Separation Status:**
  * **Robust ($\Delta_s > 0.05$):** Clear boundary gap; zero threshold ambiguity.
  * **Marginal ($0.00 \le \Delta_s \le 0.05$):** Separable at current zero threshold, but vulnerable to drift.
  * **Overlapping ($\Delta_s < 0.00$):** Overlap exists; requires threshold tuning or retraining.

