## 7. Granular Prediction Record Schema

Predictions from the evaluation run should be logged into a machine-readable CSV artifact using this column layout:

```csv
source,window,can_id,message_count,avg_interval_ms,unique_payloads,payload_entropy,label,prediction,anomaly_score,detection_latency_ms
```

### 7.1 Field Definitions & Constraints

| Column Name | Type | Valid Example | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `source` | String | `high_rate_eval_v1` | Name of the evaluated traffic source file. |
| `window` | Integer | `0` | Temporal window index ($\lfloor t / 1.0 \rfloor$). |
| `can_id` | Hex String | `0x100` | Arbitration ID monitored in this slice. |
| `message_count` | Integer | `125` | Total frames received for this ID in the window. |
| `avg_interval_ms` | Float | `7.991` | Average interval between consecutive frames (ms). |
| `unique_payloads`| Integer | `125` | Number of distinct 8-byte payload strings. |
| `payload_entropy`| Float | `6.9619` | Base-2 Shannon entropy of payload distribution. |
| `label` | String | `high_rate` | Ground-truth class (`normal`, `high_rate`, `fuzzing`). |
| `prediction` | Enum | `ANOMALY` | Model decision (`NORMAL` or `ANOMALY`). |
| `anomaly_score` | Float | `-0.042213` | Isolation Forest signed decision score. |
| `detection_latency_ms` | Float | `0.0` | Elapsed time from attack onset to this alert. |

